{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSAK9m6Ec7DmzrepTQ1F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job never reported because the script crashed on line 19, before it reached the notifier. I fixed that, plus two related problems, and wrote the causes to `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Causes**\n1. **The crash.** The script does `status=$?`, and `status` is a read-only special variable in zsh. The assignment is fatal, so the script exits before either `notify.sh` call. Your err log shows `read-only variable: status` six times, and `launchctl-print.txt` shows six runs with exit code 1. I reproduced this with the local zsh.\n2. **Claude isn't logged in under launchd.** The same log shows `Not logged in · Please run /login`. Fixing cause 1 alone would still leave every run failing.\n3. **The notifier fails silently.** If the `tg-bot` keychain lookup fails, `notify.sh` posts to a URL with an empty token and reports nothing, because `curl` isn't run with `-f`. This also covers the failure notes. The keychain lookup under launchd is unconfirmed on your machine.\n\n**Changes**\n- `bin/nightly-review.zsh`: renamed the variable to `claude_rc`. Auth now comes from `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`, read from the keychain item `claude-nightly-oauth`. Claude's stderr is logged and quoted in failure notes, and empty output counts as a failure.\n- `bin/notify.sh`: a missing token is now an error, and `curl -fsS` makes Telegram rejections non-zero.\n- I tested the original and fixed scripts in a sandbox with stub `claude`, `security`, and `curl`. Nothing touched Telegram or Anthropic, and the sandbox is removed.\n\n**What you need to do**\n1. Run `claude setup-token` in a terminal. I couldn't do this, since it's interactive and needs your subscription.\n2. Store the token: `security add-generic-password -s claude-nightly-oauth -a \"$USER\" -w`.\n3. Copy the two scripts into `~/bin/`. The plist doesn't change, and no reload is needed.\n